# Lua

Follow [LSB Development Guide — Lua](https://github.com/LandSandBoat/server/wiki/Development-Guide). 4-space indent, single quotes, LF, max 200 cols (`.editorconfig`).

- `camelCase` locals/functions. `xi.*` enums: `xi.zone`, `xi.item` (not `xi.items`), `xi.ki`, `xi.questStatus` (not bare `QUEST_AVAILABLE`).
- Enums in `scripts/enum/` attach to `xi`. Do not `require` them.
- Prefer `local`. Cached names must still convey meaning. Use `scripts/globals/npc_util.lua` helpers.
- File-private constants stay `local` (`local jobPointsMax = 500`). Do not attach one-off values to `xi.itemUtils` / `xi.*` unless other scripts need them.
- Allman multi-line tables, trailing comma. No semicolons. No extra `if` parens. No one-line `if`/`function`.
- Long conditions: `and`/`or` at end of line, `then` on its own line. `not` before, `and`/`or` after.
- NPC/mob: `---@type TNpcEntity` / `TMobEntity`, `local entity = {}`, `return entity`.
- Keep header notes. Add `!pos` when touching an NPC file. Match surrounding style; do not reformat unrelated Lua.

```lua
-- Correct
if
    condition1 and
    condition2 or
    not condition3
then
    trigger()
end

-- Wrong: extra parens, operators leading, one-liner
if (condition1)
    and condition2 then trigger() end
```
